course: dictionary
lesson: 1335
title: Plant words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A camellia is a bush, and the words around it give you clues about what it looks like. Its leaves are shiny and dark green, and its flowers are large, like roses, in pink, red or white.
explain: Words often belong to a group. A camellia is a kind of plant, and the tea plant is a kind of camellia too. When you learn one word, ask what larger group it belongs to.
explain: Read the sentence for clues. «All real tea, green, black, white and oolong, comes from one plant, Camellia sinensis» tells you that tea leaves come from a camellia, even though you may never have seen one.
fact: A camellia is a bush with shiny dark green leaves and large flowers like roses.
fact: Camellias usually have pink, red or white flowers.
fact: Camellias bloom in late winter or spring, which means their flowers open then.
fact: The tea plant is a kind of camellia, called Camellia sinensis.
fact: «Camellia» is a noun, so you can write a camellia or camellias.
exercise: «All real tea comes from one plant, Camellia sinensis.» What plant does tea come from? | A pine tree | A tulip | *A camellia | A rose bush
exercise: When do camellia flowers usually bloom? | *In late winter or spring | In autumn, when the leaves fall | In the middle of summer | At night
exercise: What do camellia flowers look like? | *Large, like roses | Tiny daisies | Blue stars | Long and thin, like grass
test: What colours are camellia flowers usually? | Green only | Blue or yellow | Black or grey | *Pink, red or white
test: Which sentence is true? | *The tea plant is a kind of camellia | Camellias have no leaves | Camellias grow only in deserts | Tea comes from a rose bush
exam: Ella reads about «The Lady of the Camellias» in English class. What kind of story is it? | *A famous old French novel | A book about tiny insects | A recipe for tea cakes | A science book about leaves
